PREDICTIONS.corrections -- controls_c6 (PREDICTIONS.txt and its addendum are never amended)
1. t_count: MIS-BUILT (see PREDICTIONS.txt.addendum).  Both derivers stopped at eval under `set -u` ("x: unbound
   variable", rc 1) because the gate's own `unknown=` arithmetic consumes `bare` before any check -- fail-closed, but it
   never reached F6's count check.  Re-aimed as t_count2 (conv_mark, which no arithmetic touches first), predicted in the
   addendum before it ran: F6 DERIVE_FAIL rc 3, F5 rc 0 printing x -- as predicted.
2. t_stub, F5: predicted "lists every grandfathered name as NEW or GONE"; measured NEW 30, GONE 0.  The stub prints every
   path as promptless, so every grandfathered probe still reads promptless (not GONE) and the 30 pty probes that detect
   the prompt read as NEW.  The prediction's substance held (no refusal, a report that is wrong in 30 names); its detail
   did not.
